 "FIX SHAPE (tier 1-2): (a) when liveness_source_ref.activation_trigger names a .github/workflows file, the watcher computes the window from the measured cadence - the p95 gap of the last N self-stamps (or gh run list) - with a floor of the nominal interval and a ceiling (e.g. 6h) so a real outage still alarms; (b) until measured data exists, default grace_multiplier 5 for GHA-triggered rows at registration; (c) the OVERDUE directive names the trigger kind and the last three delivery times so the reader can tell jitter from outage; (d) unit tests: stamps at 3h/4h/2.5h gaps with a 1h nominal interval -> not overdue; a 9h gap -> overdue; a host-task-triggered row keeps the strict 2x behaviour.",
